We are sitting in the meeting room.
It is time for our short morning meeting.
I look around at my colleagues.
Today is a special day for me.
I stand up.
I am a software engineer, and I am going to present my part of the project.
My hands are shaking a little.
But I have prepared well.
"Good morning," I say loudly.
"I have worked on the technical plan," I tell them.
"I have read all the documents."
"And I have written notes for the week's tasks."
I explain the plan to the whole team.
It is actually not difficult to talk about the technology.
Peter is sitting opposite me.
He listens and nods encouragingly.
He listens and nods.
I finish my presentation, and the others smile.
My first presentation at work has gone well.
